<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Fulani War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1804–1810</span> · Also known as Fulani jihads, Fulani jihad, jihadist campaigns of 1804–1810</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fula">Fulani</a> War, or Fulani <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jihad">jihad</a>, of 1804–1810 was the Islamic reform movement led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/usman-dan-fodio">Usman dan Fodio</a> against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hausa">Hausa</a> kingdoms. It created the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sokoto-caliphate">Sokoto Caliphate</a>, one of the largest states in nineteenth-century <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a>, and its spread destabilised neighbours including the Kanem-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bornu">Bornu Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/fulani-war.jpg" alt="Fulani War" width="320" height="154" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: AbdurRahman AbdulMoneim · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sokoto_Sultanate.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
